# CVE-2026-42504 landed in Trivy's DB on 2026-06-02 — mime.WordDecoder
# CPU-exhaustion DoS, fixed in Go 1.25.11 / 1.26.4 — authoritatively per
# the Go vuln DB GO-2026-5038 (fixed: go1.25.11, go1.26.4) and the Go
# 1.26.4 security-release announcement, NOT merely "milestone Go 1.27"
# (that is the upstream tip; the fix was backported). So our own binaries
# (now on Go 1.26.4) are patched; only the Traefik v3.6.16 binary (Go
# 1.25.0 < 1.25.11) still flags it. Re-check with the block above after
# 2026-06-15 if no Traefik release built with Go >= 1.25.11 has shipped.
# https://pkg.go.dev/vuln/GO-2026-5038
# https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-42504
CVE-2026-42504

